# Environment contract for the console (apps/console). Copy to `.env` for local development.
#
# Rules:
#   - This file documents every variable the console reads, with safe example values only.
#   - Real values never enter git. `.env` and every other `.env.*` file are ignored.
#   - Add a variable here in the same change that adds it to the config module.
#   - Secrets also accept NAME_FILE=/path/to/file so container secret mounts work.
#   - Hosted deployments inject these from the platform's secret store; nothing is baked into the image.
#   - Commented-out lines show the built-in default. An empty value means "not set".

NODE_ENV=development
LOG_LEVEL=info

# HTTP listener of the `api` role, and how long shutdown waits for requests in flight.
# HOST=0.0.0.0
PORT=11199
# SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS=20

# Behind a reverse proxy or a load balancer (deploy/README.md, "Behind a reverse proxy").
# Keep idle connections open longer than the proxy does, and bound how long one request may take
# to arrive.
# HTTP_KEEP_ALIVE_SECONDS=65
# HTTP_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=60
# One log line per request. Turn it off when the proxy already keeps this log.
# ACCESS_LOG=true
# Peers whose forwarding headers are believed: addresses or CIDR networks, comma-separated.
# Empty means nobody's are, and the client address is the address of the peer.
# TRUSTED_PROXIES=127.0.0.1,::1
# Where a trusted proxy puts the client address and its request id. `x-forwarded-for` is read as
# a chain; any other header as a single address.
# CLIENT_IP_HEADER=x-forwarded-for
# REQUEST_ID_HEADER=x-request-id

# PostgreSQL, the one stateful dependency. The local database of deploy/compose.dev.yaml:
DATABASE_URL=postgres://console:console-dev-only@127.0.0.1:5433/console
# DATABASE_POOL_MAX=10
# The authority the database's certificate is checked against, as PEM (one certificate or a
# bundle), where the platform's authority is its own, as a managed database's is: the chain and
# the host name are both verified, as sslmode=verify-full does. DATABASE_CA_FILE reads it from a
# file instead. With it, DATABASE_URL carries no ssl parameters of its own.
# DATABASE_CA=

# What the board is called, on its pages and wherever the console names itself. Conventionally the
# organization or the person it is for, then Console, as SkillCDN Console is named: Acme Console.
# The workspace row is made at boot and renamed from here.
# WORKSPACE_NAME=Console

# A single-container install has no `worker`: set this and the `api` role carries the worker's
# work (the sweep of what time has ended) itself.
# WORKER_IN_PROCESS=false

# How many days after a task was done or dropped, and last touched, the console puts it away
# (ADR-0029): out of the board and the lists, open by its number. 0 never puts a task away.
# TASK_ARCHIVE_AFTER_DAYS=30

# How many hours a run goes unheard, and not waiting for an answer, before the console ends it
# as abandoned (ADR-0041): an agent closed with its terminal leaves no run open for ever. 0 never
# ends a run.
# RUN_ENDED_AFTER_HOURS=24

# Signing in (deploy/README.md, "Signing in"). People sign in through GitHub, Google, or both:
# set a provider's client id and secret, AUTH_SECRET and PUBLIC_URL together, or none of them.
# Unset: nobody signs in, and the board is nobody's.
# The origin people use, where a provider sends them back to: PUBLIC_URL/auth/gh/callback and
# PUBLIC_URL/auth/google/callback are the callback URLs. Without a path.
# PUBLIC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11199
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# The app's client secret (GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE reads it from a file instead).
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# What a sign-in in flight is sealed with: at least 32 characters, the same on every replica
# (AUTH_SECRET_FILE reads it from a file).
# AUTH_SECRET=
# The first administrators: logins at GitHub, addresses at Google, comma-separated. Let in when
# they sign in, by this alone, and made administrators then; an administrator lets everyone else
# in on the People page, and may make or unmake other administrators there.
# ADMINS=
# A Workspace domain whose accounts are all in, as Google vouches for them at sign-in.
# GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_DOMAIN=
# Where people use the git host in a browser, and where its API is. GitHub Enterprise Server:
# https://<host> and https://<host>/api/v3.
# GITHUB_WEB_URL=https://github.com
# GITHUB_API_URL=https://api.github.com
# The organization at GitHub whose members are all in, read through a GitHub App installed on it
# with the organization permission Members, read-only: the app's id (or its client id), its
# private key as PEM (GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE reads it from a file instead), and the
# organization's login. All three or none, with the GitHub client above. Asked at sign-in, and
# read whole by the worker every ten minutes.
# GITHUB_APP_ID=
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=
# GITHUB_ORG=
# Google (Workspace): an OAuth client of the web application type, with
# PUBLIC_URL/auth/google/callback as an authorized redirect URI (GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE reads
# the secret from a file instead).
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# How long a browser stays signed in without being used.
# SESSION_TTL_DAYS=30
# The most days a token for an agent may be good for, when the organization requires an expiry.
# Unset: a person chooses, up to a year or never.
# TOKEN_DAYS_AT_MOST=

# The default UI: a directory with a build of apps/console/web (`pnpm build` writes it to
# apps/console/web/dist); the container image brings one and sets this. Unset: no UI, API only.
# While working on the UI you do not need it: `pnpm dev:web` serves the UI by itself.
# WEB_ROOT=apps/console/web/dist

# The organization's skills (docs/architecture.md, "Built on SkillCDN, not inside it"): the
# SkillCDN deployment they are read through, and their address there, as the standard spells one
# (/gh/<owner>/<repo>, with @<ref> and a path when needed). A project may name an address of its
# own on its Settings page; this one is shown for a project that names none. Unset: such a
# project's Skills page says there is no address yet.
# SKILLCDN_URL=https://skillcdn.ai
# SKILLS_ADDRESS=/gh/acme/skills
# A pack served from a machine (/local/<owner>/<name>, docs/adr/0031-the-console-reads-a-pack-as-the-skillcdn-command-does-and-a-local-one-from-a-directory.md)
# is read from this directory, laid out as <owner>/<name>, with the reading rules a deployment
# applies and no deployment asked. The image sets /app/packs, where the console's own pack is at
# skillcdn/console, and an organization mounts its packs beside it. Unset: a local address is
# not found.
# SKILLS_DIR=

# The bucket files go to, through the S3 API (docs/adr/0016-the-bucket-is-reached-through-the-s3-api-with-the-consoles-own-signing-and-reads-what-the-rows-kept-before-it.md):
# the store's origin and the bucket, both or neither, and how requests are signed: with the pair
# of keys (S3_CREDENTIALS=keys, the default), or with the credentials the platform hands the
# container at an endpoint of its own, named by the platform's own variables and renewed by it
# (S3_CREDENTIALS=platform, docs/adr/0018-the-bucket-may-be-reached-with-the-credentials-the-platform-hands-the-container.md).
# Unset: the bytes of files are kept in PostgreSQL. With them: the region the signature names
# (us-east-1 where the store has none), the token that comes with temporary keys, what every key
# begins with, and whether the bucket is in the path (every store) or in the host (some).
# S3_ENDPOINT=https://s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com
# S3_BUCKET=console-files
# S3_CREDENTIALS=keys
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# The secret of the pair (S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY_FILE reads it from a file instead).
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# S3_REGION=us-east-1
# S3_SESSION_TOKEN=
# S3_KEY_PREFIX=
# S3_PATH_STYLE=true
# The local store of deploy/compose.dev.yaml, where the integration tests make the bucket:
# S3_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:7070
# S3_BUCKET=console
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=console
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=console-dev-only
